# Agent working agreements

## Docs

The Unity project is `E:\Projects\Unity\unity-gem-td`.
All design and planning docs live in:
`E:\Projects\Docs\project-docs-unity-gem-td\Unity\unity-gem-td`.

Read `HOME.md` first, then `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` before assuming a decision is
missing. Use the canonical owner for the subject:

1. `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` — what the build does today
2. `GDD.md` — gameplay rules and scope
3. `ARCHITECTURE.md` — code boundaries and runtime contracts
4. `UI-SPEC.md` — presentation and interaction contracts
5. `DAMAGE-MODEL.md` — combat and damage rules
6. `ROADMAP.md` — what to build next and the current gate
7. `TEST_STRATEGY.md` — done criteria and verification reporting

`planning/STATUS.md` and `planning/handoff.md` hold the existing phase and
release-scope detail. `planning/sdd/` is the SDD ledger. Historical plans are
not a work list: Phase 2 and PR6 plans are closed, and the full catalog is out
of the current Demo / Early Access version.

If a note disagrees with a living owner, the living owner wins. Do not add
design docs, plans, or SDD scratch to the Unity repository. Do not duplicate
the docs tree in the game repo.

Do not `git commit` or `git push` unless the user explicitly asks to commit
or push. Sync, update, finalize, record, save, and "docs first" do not
authorize either one. The docs checkout is a git repo and the same rule
applies there. Writing or updating docs is not a commit request.

Change only what the user names. If that change would alter something unnamed
through a shared path, keep the unnamed behavior as it is. Do not edit its
values, and do not restructure it when the named change would not reach it.
Card-chrome colors and tag-chip colors are independent. Do not rewrite an
asset in a way that drops or resets values the user set. Script defaults are
not those values.

Stay inside the current `ROADMAP.md` gate. A class, imported asset, or passing
EditMode suite does not close a gate; the documented runtime or manual exit
must be verified.

## Screenshots

Do not capture, generate, or save screenshots during normal workflow. Verify
scenes through hierarchy/component inspection, camera settings, serialized
bindings, and the Unity console. Do not add `Assets/Screenshots`.

## References

Look up this project in its docs repo first. For external guidance, search SCE
for `unity-gem-td`, then retrieve the needed document. Use Context7 for
library/API documentation and do not treat training memory as API evidence.
